&lt;p&gt;Test Log -T-92563-OC5032&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cross-SCP Termination Testing for SCP-5942&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to the highly aggressive, unpredictable, and intelligent nature of SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
, termination testing has been ordered, with clearance from O5 Command. With major concerns raised about possible developed immunities (due to the failure of SCP-409) and other possible immunity, all tests must first be carried out on tissue and/or scale samples taken from SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
unless it is non-anomalous objects, if done with non-anomalous objects on tissue SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
can still gain Immunity. This step may be bypassed only by O5 Command order.&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-252500-1&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-063&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tissue Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Sample eradicated. Little to No traces above molecular level remain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Termination Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
SCP-063 was refitted to the end of a robots arm, which was deployed into 5942&#039;s enclosure, during that time SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
was scarred and had some exposed tissues. Initial approach failed, the damage done to SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
&#039;s body before regeneration overtakes the destruction process. Newly regrown scales are not vulnerable to SCP-063&#039;s eradication effect: 5942&lt;br /&gt;
destroys the deployment arm and 063 digs a hole through the enclosure&#039;s ground, where it is later recovered. 5942&lt;br /&gt;
succeeds in extending digging through the hole and maiming 9 security personnel before containment is reestablished.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hypothesis:&lt;/strong&gt;82 is not bound to base Earth biological chemistry and it&#039;s scales are &#039;inorganic&#039;. Some of the D-class were arguing whether to even call it a &#039;living&#039; creature, at least as we understand life. This worries me, because an unliving, undying intelligent monster that can control the planet and solar system… well, that&#039;s a &lt;strong&gt;XK&lt;/strong&gt; class extinction event waiting to happen. -Agent ██████&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-173&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tissue Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
N/A, overridden by O5-Command&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Termination Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
SCP-173 introduced into the containment area of SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
. SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
makes screeches several times, and tries to kill SCP-173 and blasted SCP-173&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notes: After review, it appears SCP-173 was unable to do lethal damage to SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
due to a major difference in physical size. A possible repeat of this test may be made if SCP-5942&lt;br /&gt;
was damaged enough to reduce its physical mass to a level equal with SCP-173.&lt;/p&gt;
