&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Researcher:&lt;/strong&gt; Dr. [Redacted]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-682&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tissue Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Denied by O5 Command.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Termination Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
SCP-682 was brought into SCP-5942&#039;s old containment area/Testing chamber, screams of the two entities continue for 4 days, at which point the noise abruptly stops. Video feeds reveal SCP-682 with 99% of its initial mass absent and huddled in the southwest corner. Feed shows SCP-5942 on the east end of the room with about 30% its initial mass absent. SCP-5942 was regenerating from injuries and SCP-682 is displaying signs of being infected with AML F7437, and laughing as if it was in euphoria.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When SCP-5942 was asked &amp;quot;how was your encounter&amp;quot; with SCP-682 SCP-5942 will react with rage.&lt;br /&gt;
SCP-5942 was asked why it reacted with rage when 682 was mentioned and resulted in a containment breach (seven-thousandth occurrence) with in heavy casualties.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Note: Dr. [Redacted] was terminated for disobeying orders from O5 Command and 682 and 5942 was not to be Cross-tested, the one who gave the order to Cross-test will be terminated or punished severely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-173 with a photograph of SCP-096&#039;s face attached to it&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tissue Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
N/A&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Termination Test Record:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Denied by O5-██&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notes: No. Hell NO. Setting aside the problem of the SCP-682 and SCP-5942 Cross test, a SCP-173 that cannot be observed for fear of triggering a response from SCP-096 is a self-perpetuating catastrophe that the Foundation does not, under any reasonable circumstances, have the slightest desire to unleash and 5942 will probably let all the other anomalies at Site 19 out. Denied with vehemence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
